00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:58.810
<b>Most
Common
Entrance
Exam
Math
Problems</b>

00:16:11.140 --> 00:16:14.670
I'm bored. What should I do?

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:20.070
Oh, it's pretty late already.

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:22.580
I need to start working on dinner.

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:26.960
What should I make?

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:30.510
Something original that'll 
surprise Natsumi...

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:35.370
I should start with an appetizer, 
like in French cuisine.

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:36.960
Some hors d'oeuvres!

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:41.460
And I can put a Japanese spin 
on it by using gyoza...

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.770
Those are hard to make, though...

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:50.480
Oh, I need to see what 
ingredients we have first.

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:57.120
Curry it is, then.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:03.000
I-It's not like I'm compromising. 
Everyone likes curry.

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:05.490
And it comes in lots of different types,

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:09.330
so if I just make my idea of 
perfect curry, it'll be fine!

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:12.300
Okay, I'll start cutting 
the vegetables first.

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:39.900
Darn it! I hate onions! 
They're killing my eyes!

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:42.170
I can't even hum anymore!

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:46.100
Fine. I'll just put the 
onions in and nothing else.

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:49.870
That took a lot of effort. 
I'm sure they'll understand.

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:50.660
Huh?

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:53.210
The curry pot's already out.

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:57.510
Isn't this yesterday's meat and potato stew?

00:17:57.740 --> 00:18:00.890
That's it! I can use this!

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:03.440
It already has basically 
everything that goes in curry!

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:05.020
I can just heat it up!

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:06.340
This'll work!

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:09.150
Wh-What a fantastic idea!

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:12.350
Even a pro wouldn't have come up with that!

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:15.300
The sweetness of the stew 
will make the curry richer!

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:16.470
It's a dream collaboration!

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:21.860
And to make it even richer, I can add 
honey... except we don't have any, so...

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:24.360
All right! I'll put in a ton of sugar!

00:18:24.840 --> 00:18:27.960
I have a feeling this is gonna be amazing!

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:31.260
Sugar, sugar... huh? The sugar's gone...

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:34.130
That's weird. Where's the sugar?

00:18:34.270 --> 00:18:38.580
Wow, the sugar's attracting a ton of ants.

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:40.640
This isn't good.

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:43.800
I can't make amazing curry without sugar.

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:48.260
What do I do? If there's no sugar...

00:18:48.470 --> 00:18:51.430
I have to make an amazing meal,

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:54.220
or Natsumi will just make fun of me...

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:56.690
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

00:18:56.980 --> 00:19:01.490
<i>Curry filled with sugar? 
Would that even be good?</i>

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:04.690
<i>Actually, why did I decide to cook at all?</i>

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:07.780
<i>I wanted to make something 
great and show up Natsumi,</i>

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:10.660
<i>but if it tastes bad, there's no point...</i>

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:14.920
Huh? What's that smell?

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.370
Oh, no! There's smoke coming from the pot!

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:21.710
G-G-G-Gotta do something! Um, um! Fire!

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:25.140
What on earth are you doing?

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:27.080
It's only a little scorched.

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:29.060
All you need to do is turn off the heat.

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:31.980
This amount of charring is no big deal.

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.820
Just put water in it,

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:36.350
then add the curry roux, and you're done.

00:19:36.810 --> 00:19:38.210
On low heat.

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.300
Well, I'll be in the living room.

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:41.860
Call me if you need anything.

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:46.790
M-Mom!

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:56.790
I want to make really good curry... 
so I'd like your help after all.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.130
Of course.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:25.620
<b>Maruin Milk 
</b>Non-homogenized

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:13.950
Here you go! Dinner is served!

00:21:16.680 --> 00:21:19.050
Well, it <i>looks</i> like curry...

00:21:20.270 --> 00:21:22.380
What? Aren't you going to eat?

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:24.650
I mean, I'll eat it, but...

00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:31.410
I-It's curry!

00:21:31.410 --> 00:21:34.020
Nee-chan made it, but it 
actually tastes like curry!

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:36.410
It doesn't "taste like" curry. It <i>is</i> curry.

00:21:36.410 --> 00:21:37.730
Did you do something to it?

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:38.680
Not really.

00:21:38.680 --> 00:21:40.750
I just made some good curry.

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:42.810
That doesn't answer my question!

00:21:42.810 --> 00:21:44.560
Also, is there more?!

00:21:44.560 --> 00:21:49.330
There is, but I haven't had any 
yet, so don't eat it all now!

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:00.210
Yum!

00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:04.760
<b>Non Non Biyori</b>

00:22:06.510 --> 00:22:13.300
<b>That's all for today</b>

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:34.220
Sweet! I got more New Year's 
money than I thought!

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:37.280
Now I can live like the Tokyo bourgeoisie!

00:23:36.530 --> 00:23:39.510
I do have New Year's money 
for you, actually...

00:23:39.510 --> 00:23:40.950
I just realized something.

00:23:40.950 --> 00:23:42.380
Oh, did you now, Renge-dono?

00:23:42.380 --> 00:23:43.450
Rattle, rattle.

00:23:43.450 --> 00:23:44.290
Oh, Director!

00:23:44.290 --> 00:23:45.180
Time to operate!

00:23:45.180 --> 00:23:46.940
It's snowing like crazy!

00:23:46.940 --> 00:23:50.950
<b>Episode 10</b>

00:23:46.940 --> 00:23:50.950
<b>It Got Cold and Then Hot</b>

00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:54.410
Photo: Nolcalus

00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:54.410
<b>Please Watch Again</b>

00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:54.410
<b>Nonstop</b>
